            0.124
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Summary"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.144,
            0.885,
            0.202
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Objects are made from a large variety of materials. An object can be made up of a single material or a combination of different materials."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.205,
            0.883,
            0.243
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " We can use different materials to make objects with similar functions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.248,
            0.883,
            0.285
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " The method of arranging objects into groups is called classification."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.289,
            0.883,
            0.328
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Materials possess different properties which determine their use."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.331,
            0.883,
            0.371
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Materials are grouped or classified based on their similarities or differences in their properties."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.374,
            0.884,
            0.43
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Materials can be grouped based on appearance, such as lustrous or non-lustrous and based on the feel, such as hard or soft."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.435,
            0.883,
            0.474
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Materials are grouped as transparent, translucent or opaque depending on how much we can see through them."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.476,
            0.882,
            0.514
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Some materials are soluble in water, while others remain insoluble."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.518,
            0.879,
            0.539
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Anything that occupies space and has mass is called matter."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.542,
            0.724,
            0.561
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " The space occupied by matter is its volume."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.564,
            0.868,
            0.584
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Mass quantifies the amount of matter present in an object."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.49,
            0.622,
            0.65,
            0.647
          ],
